 ## Overview
-Gaussian Pruning (Monocular) is a preprocessing step for 3D Gaussian Splatting initialization in monocular SLAM that filters out unreliable initial Gaussian centers based on multi-view consistency checks [S1, S2, unofficial]. It prevents incorrect initial geometry from degrading camera tracking performance by ensuring only Gaussians with valid, consistent observations in the training views are retained [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that focus on replication or allocation density, this method focuses on quality control of the initial point cloud [S1, unofficial].
+Gaussian Pruning (Monocular) is a preprocessing step for 3D Gaussian Splatting initialization in monocular SLAM that filters out unreliable initial Gaussian centers based on per-view projection and visibility checks [S1, S2, unofficial]. It prevents incorrect initial geometry from degrading camera tracking performance by ensuring only Gaussians with valid, consistent observations in the training views are retained [S1, unofficial]. Unlike sibling methods that focus on replication or allocation density, this method focuses on quality control of the initial point cloud [S1, unofficial].
 
